    "tStartMs": 31090,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Hey, this is Henry I am here today to share with you a very special announcement something"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 35250,
    "dDurationMs": 4739,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I'm really excited about we have a new series or at least a pilot for new series"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 39989,
    "dDurationMs": 2459,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And I hope you will be willing to go check it out"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 42449,
    "dDurationMs": 4830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's over on an online streaming platform called Verve, which has a lot of other long-form, shows as well"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 47280,
    "dDurationMs": 6090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They approached us and asked us to develop a show so I worked with the minute earth team and Derek Muller of veritasium to make"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 53829,
    "dDurationMs": 2810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Paradigms here is a clip that you can watch"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 57430,
    "dDurationMs": 3259,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the philosopher Plato suggested that sight was a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 61089,
    "dDurationMs": 6650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "visual fire that melded with daylight somehow allowing the forms of objects to travel long distances and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 67930,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Into the observers eye now Plato was pretty vague on the details"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 71680,
    "dDurationMs": 5239,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the basic idea of visual fire rang true for people for a number of reasons"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 77500,
    "dDurationMs": 5269,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Animals eyes seemed to gleam at night and people often appear to have a twinkle in their eye"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 83170,
    "dDurationMs": 5300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Plus everyone knew that a gaze could have certain mystical powers from that eerie feeling"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 88600,
    "dDurationMs": 4279,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You get when you know that you're being watched to a Lover's"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 93280,
    "dDurationMs": 4129,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Enchantment to the evil eye the idea that you can harm somebody"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 97659,
    "dDurationMs": 7610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Just by looking at them even back then people did realize there were problems with the visual rays"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 105700,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Understanding of vision like when I opened my eyes at night"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 108909,
    "dDurationMs": 4040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If beams have to shoot out and travel all the way to the Stars and back"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 113380,
    "dDurationMs": 8000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "How am I able to see the stars right away or why can't we see things in the dark does darkness somehow stop those?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 121540,
    "dDurationMs": 4129,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Visual rays, but the thing about mental models of the world about paradigms"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 125670,
    "dDurationMs": 5550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Is that it's really tough to kill an established theory especially one that makes a lot of intuitive sense"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 131500,
    "dDurationMs": 3529,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Just by pointing out its weaknesses you have to have an alternative"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 135340,
    "dDurationMs": 4459,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That can explain at least as much more compellingly and with fewer problems"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 141129,
    "dDurationMs": 5720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So as you can see paradigms is a show about how we know what we know the first episode is about the science of sight"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 146950,
    "dDurationMs": 5580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "About how we used to think sight worked and vision worked, and how we now understand it has more to do with the brain then"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 153200,
    "dDurationMs": 5509,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We originally thought the important things to know are one. You can go watch this for free right now over on Verve"
